---
// What travels over signaling and what travels over the peer connection, side by side.
---
<figure class="path-manifest" aria-labelledby="path-manifest-title">
  <div class="diagram-head"><h3 id="path-manifest-title">Two paths, two kinds of message</h3></div>
  <div class="manifest-drawers">
    <section class="manifest-drawer setup" aria-labelledby="manifest-setup">
      <p class="manifest-plate" id="manifest-setup">Signaling</p>
      <p class="manifest-route">WebSocket to the Cloudflare Worker and room Durable Object</p>
      <ul>
        <li>SDP offer and answer</li>
        <li>ICE candidates</li>
        <li>Connection metadata</li>
        <li>Invitation authentication</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="manifest-when">Used to introduce the browsers</p>
    </section>
    <section class="manifest-drawer game" aria-labelledby="manifest-game">
      <p class="manifest-plate" id="manifest-game">Data channel</p>
      <p class="manifest-route">Encrypted, ordered <code>playkit-v1</code> channel between the host and one guest</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Seat requests</li>
        <li>Game actions</li>
        <li>Authoritative snapshots, including cards and bets</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="manifest-when">Used for the game once the channel opens</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <figcaption>The invitation starts in the URL fragment, which browsers don’t send to the web host. The phone then sends it in the signaling handshake; the signaling service stores only its SHA-256 digest.</figcaption>
</figure>
